# Line endings are content here, not formatting.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default on Windows, and with no rule in this file
# it rewrites every text file in the working tree to CRLF. That is invisible in
# most repositories and is not invisible in this one: `tools-pennsync-migrate`
# sends a migration's text to Postgres, which stores a function's body verbatim,
# and the hosted comparison reads `md5(prosrc)`. Applying four migrations from a
# Windows checkout on 2026-09-23 wrote `\r\n` into eight function bodies, and
# the store then differed from every store built here while the ledger recorded
# both as having run the same file.
#
# `tools-pennsync-migration-fingerprints` and the generated-SQL tests hash file
# content too, so they fail wholesale on such a checkout rather than pointing at
# this.
#
# This protects a checkout made after it lands. `readMigrations` undoes CRLF as
# well, for the ones made before.
* text=auto eol=lf

